Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Depends: python3
Recommends: gnome-shell, dconf-cli, oneplus-erhai-sensors
Filename: ./oneplus-erhai-desktop_1.9_all.deb
Size: 53200
MD5sum: da66b2dd39165a60ac62dcb46fe65c1e
SHA1: f5c0c8f612ce4fd4f2bfbad9c45cd68e930dc58e
SHA256: d05e5ccb83d9d0252f95ae01ad3074107b156322ce0c47a4af836d35e976d056
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Description: Desktop glue for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 Everything the GNOME desktop needs on top of the base image: bringing up the
 Adreno 830 GMU before session start (erhai-gpu-pin; the GPU is PINNED
 always-active at runtime-PM 'on' on every kernel since 2026-09-13 — it never
 runtime-suspends, so the intermittent GMU resume hang can never fire),
 boot-time GL environment selection
 (erhai-desktop-gl), power-key REAL panel power cycle
 (erhai-power-toggle + erhai-power-watch.py -> erhai-panel-power.sh: parks the
 GPU then tears the internal DPU/DSI panel down via gnome-shell SetActive, so
 compiles/downloads/external-display apps keep running while the panel sleeps;
 backlight-only toggle while a DP-1 external monitor is attached; ships
 suspend.target MASKED — GNOME never offers the b29 s2idle POR-lottery),
 pogo keyboard attach/detach -> OSK on/off (erhai-pogo-osk +
 erhai-pogo-osk.py), folio folded onto the screen -> panel backlight
 off/on (erhai-folio-gate.service starts/stops erhai-folio-fold.py with the
 keyboard attach state; erhai-folio-calibrate + erhai-folio-probe.py pick the
 fold signal and write /etc/erhai/folio-fold.conf), the shared backlight
 on/off/toggle script both features use (erhai-display-toggle.sh, which also
 plays a panel-off click on every blank and a panel-on click on every restore
 through the active session via pw-play; /etc/erhai/display.conf can mute or
 replace either), ktz8868
 backlight display toggle, USB-C host charging while acting as data
 host (erhai-host-charge), pogo keyboard activation helper + launcher,
 Novatek NT36536 touchscreen bring-up before GDM (erhai-touchscreen +
 touch-calibration udev rule), dconf defaults, and the desktop-users /
 user-groups helpers used by image presets.

